From: Vijay Balaji <vijbal@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 16:37:45 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] rootdisk: Increase F2FS_MINSIZE threshold for 3GB rootfs

HLOS has increased the rootfs GPT partition size from 128MB to 3GB.
Rootdisk driver fails to format ovelay whenever the rootfs partition exceeds
F2FS_MINSIZE. Once the partition grew past the old 150MB threshold, it leaves the
overlay unformatted and forcing a tmpfs fallback at boot.

Raising F2FS_MINSIZE to the new rootfs partition size (3GB) so it never exceeds
the threshold and mkfs.ext4 is always used for the first-time overlay format.

Change-Id: Idfbf0705d8b6827032782e43767b21df9a66a869
Signed-off-by: Vijay Balaji <vijbal@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
Index: fstools-2024.07.14~408c2cc4/libfstools/common.h
===================================================================
--- fstools-2024.07.14~408c2cc4.orig/libfstools/common.h
+++ fstools-2024.07.14~408c2cc4/libfstools/common.h
@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@
 #include "libfstools.h"
 #include "volume.h"

-#define F2FS_MINSIZE		(150ULL * 1024ULL * 1024ULL)
+#define F2FS_MINSIZE		(3000ULL * 1024ULL * 1024ULL)

 int read_uint_from_file(char *dirname, char *filename, unsigned int *i);
 char *read_string_from_file(const char *dirname, const char *filename, char *buf, size_t bufsz);
